  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Facilitating Voluntary Returns in Iraq to Support Durable Solutions for Internally Displaced Persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM is proposing to support IDPs minority groups to attain access to durable solutions pathways, with a focus on protection and MHPSS support. This project IOM aims to support organizations that further facilitate key mechanisms that support the transition from a humanitarian response through supporting systems that enable recovery for the Yazidi population, in line with Yazidi and Government of Japan priorities. As well as facilitating the return for IDPs and supporting them pre- and post-departure through a variety of programs. This action will be implemented in parallel with other IOM&#x2019;s interventions in the target areas, seeking to obtain a comprehensive, multi-sectoral approach to addressing the displacement-related vulnerabilities of the population targeted by this project.Under the proposed project, IOM&#x2019;s work will be centred in Dohuk and Ninewa within the context of return (FVM) and reintegration, as these are areas that continue to confront huge displacement needs. Geographically, the proposed project will thus target communities in Ninewa Governorate which has been severely impacted by forced and premature closure displacement sites and still hosts significant numbers of IDPs, mostly living in informal sites and urban areas, particularly across Mosul, Tel Afar, Ba&#x2019;aj and Sinjar districts.</narrative>
  </description>
